  "method": "paper-counts",
  "method_note": "ICRA 2026 (Vienna, 1–5 Jun 2026) uses a mostly interactive format: the PaperPlaza program lists only 24 titled oral sessions (20 Regular + 4 Award Finalist, 216 papers); 2604 papers sit in 6 untitled 'Interactive Session' blocks plus 131 Late Breaking Results. Session titles therefore cover only ~7% of papers, so paper-level counts were used instead. Counted: the FIRST (primary) author-selected IEEE RAS keyword of every program entry that lists keywords in the PaperPlaza content lists (2898 of 2951 entries, incl. oral, award, interactive and LBR papers). Each of 230 distinct RAS keywords was mapped by hand to 1 taxonomy id (or split 50/50 across 2); 71 papers whose primary keyword has no taxonomy fit (e.g. Simulation and Animation, Performance Evaluation and Benchmarking, software/architecture keywords) were excluded, leaving 2827. Because RAS keywords have no foundation-model term, any paper whose title matches VLA/VLM/LLM/vision-language/language model/foundation model (165 papers) is split 0.5 foundation-models + 0.5 its keyword topic. Weights = paper-equivalents / 2827; ids below 0.02 omitted (estimation 0.014, space-robotics 0.009 = 25 paper-equivalents, primary keyword 'Space Robotics and Automation'; one oral session was titled 'Field and Space Robotics', phm, education). Mapping is the dataset author's judgement, not ICRA's.",
